Z||000000||V8Fiero||05-20-2001||04:19 PM||||ok,<P>Heres whats going on.<P>With the thermostat car heats up almost immediately and goes into the red. Without it it will take a long time before the heat starts to climb.<P>Radiator isnt clogged.<BR>Coolant sensor switch good.<BR>New thermostat.<P>I noticed after it started to run hot, I touched the coolant tube going into the radiatior. It was cold.<P>New water pump is in order I believe. <BR>What do you think?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Topknot||05-20-2001||04:55 PM||||Hallo V8Fiero,<P>I had excatly the same problem on my 85 SE 4 a few years ago and ended up cracking the head due to overheating and loosing all my coolant and pouring in water while stuck in the city.<P>It worked out that even with the thermostat out, (The only way to stop the sudden heat rising) it would still heat up but not as fast being that water was able to get thru a bit, but eventually I replaced the water pump and all problems of water movement were solved.<P>Topknot =]<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||05-20-2001||06:54 PM||||With a COLD engine, remove the cap for the thermostat housing...<BR>Start the engine and see if the coolant flows out!<BR>If it doesn't flow, bad pump...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000003||V8Fiero||05-20-2001||08:08 PM||||Just replaced the water pump. Did the trick!!!!<P>Thanks guys<BR>Scott||||reg||1
